# One ARP request, 42 bytes, as the Linux kernel put it on a TAP device.
#
# ⚠ Captured, not written by hand. If this file is ever regenerated, capture it
# again — a frame typed out from memory is not a fixture (`CLAUDE.md` §1).
#
# How it was captured:
#   Arch Linux, kernel 7.0.2-arch1-1, x86_64, 2026-08-26
#   unshare -Urn (no sudo), tap0 with the default MTU of 1500
#   ip addr add 10.0.0.1/24 dev tap0; ip link set tap0 up
#   ping -c 3 -i 0.3 -W 1 10.0.0.2
#   the first frame read whose bytes 12..13 were 08 06
#
# The source hardware address is whatever the kernel picked for tap0 on that
# run; it is different on the next one, which is why this file is a recording
# and the checks never expect it to be reproduced.
#
# ⚠ Nothing in this repository parses these bytes yet. The check that uses this
# file asserts how they are printed, not what they mean.
ff ff ff ff ff ff 9e 28 ea ff 03 06 08 06 00 01
08 00 06 04 00 01 9e 28 ea ff 03 06 0a 00 00 01
00 00 00 00 00 00 0a 00 00 02
